WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:01.260 --> 00:00:05.850
So in the world of boxing, if an opponent
knows what to anticipate from his opponent,

00:00:05.850 --> 00:00:07.050
he has an edge.

00:00:07.050 --> 00:00:13.560
In war, if a country facing another enemy
can anticipate which side that enemy's going

00:00:13.560 --> 00:00:16.430
to attack from, this person has an edge.

00:00:16.430 --> 00:00:23.120
If YOU, the entrepreneur, can anticipate what
you are guaranteed to face in the world of

00:00:23.120 --> 00:00:25.160
business, you have an edge.

00:00:25.160 --> 00:00:31.119
So my goal today is to give you an edge over
everybody else who doesn't watch this video.

00:00:31.119 --> 00:00:33.650
And you're smart, watching this Valuetainment
video here with me.

00:00:33.650 --> 00:00:37.969
So, ten challenges every entrepreneur will
face.

00:00:37.969 --> 00:00:42.979
#1: You've got to learn the 9 - 5 sacrificing
your salary.

00:00:42.979 --> 00:00:43.979
That is a challenge you're going to face.

00:00:43.979 --> 00:00:47.899
Let me tell you, when you go from having a
salary that's coming in, it's warm, it's fuzzy,

00:00:47.899 --> 00:00:51.410
it's a nice, comfortable pillow, you've got
benefits, you've got all this stuff, and you

00:00:51.410 --> 00:00:55.139
say, "I'm going to be an entrepreneur," you
have to sacrifice your salary.

00:00:55.139 --> 00:00:59.440
Benefits, health insurance, no matter what
income, worst case scenario, you're going

00:00:59.440 --> 00:01:00.499
to make your five grand a month.

00:01:00.499 --> 00:01:02.600
Worse case you're going to make your eight
grand a month.

00:01:02.600 --> 00:01:04.100
That is out the window.

00:01:04.100 --> 00:01:07.110
You will have to anticipate this happening.

00:01:07.110 --> 00:01:10.460
Next, is your capital management.

00:01:10.460 --> 00:01:12.760
What do I mean by capital management?

00:01:12.760 --> 00:01:16.950
Time clock, on how much you've saved, and
what your expenses are, you're going to hear

00:01:16.950 --> 00:01:20.210
it constantly tick tock, tick tock, tick tock.

00:01:20.210 --> 00:01:25.570
The way you manage your capital will allow
you to stay in business long enough to make

00:01:25.570 --> 00:01:30.490
it as a business owner if you know how to
manage your capital properly.

00:01:30.490 --> 00:01:34.240
It doesn't matter if you're a real estate
agent, if you're a technology company out

00:01:34.240 --> 00:01:37.010
of Silicon Valley, or if you're running a
liquor store.

00:01:37.010 --> 00:01:42.550
You will need to know how to manage your capital
yourself to stretch it out as long as possible.

00:01:42.550 --> 00:01:43.760
Next, processing issues.

00:01:43.760 --> 00:01:45.130
This looks pretty bad.

00:01:45.130 --> 00:01:46.990
This looks like a horror movie right here.

00:01:46.990 --> 00:01:48.370
Luis, this looks pretty intense.

00:01:48.370 --> 00:01:50.030
It says, solve for x.

00:01:50.030 --> 00:01:52.030
Let me tell you what that is.

00:01:52.030 --> 00:01:58.670
You will have to process many unknown issues
that you've never experienced before.

00:01:58.670 --> 00:02:00.360
You've never experienced before.

00:02:00.360 --> 00:02:01.360
How do you do this?

00:02:01.360 --> 00:02:02.360
I don't know how to work this part.

00:02:02.360 --> 00:02:04.000
I don't know how to handle this issue before.

00:02:04.000 --> 00:02:07.659
I never knew I needed this insurance policy
to be able to do this event at a hotel.

00:02:07.659 --> 00:02:11.519
I never knew my requirement to be able to
get a lease in a building was this that I

00:02:11.519 --> 00:02:13.189
have to spend another $7,000.

00:02:13.189 --> 00:02:16.980
I never knew I needed to do this other part
that's going to cost me $17,000.

00:02:16.980 --> 00:02:19.530
How come nobody told me about this stuff before?

00:02:19.530 --> 00:02:20.590
Anticipation.

00:02:20.590 --> 00:02:21.590
It's going to happen.

00:02:21.590 --> 00:02:25.920
So if you don't know how to solve for x, these
situations you're going to go in, you're going

00:02:25.920 --> 00:02:26.950
to have a hard time with it.

00:02:26.950 --> 00:02:31.120
But you need to anticipate there will be many
issues, unknown issues, that you need to solve

00:02:31.120 --> 00:02:33.150
that no one else is going to prepare you for.

00:02:33.150 --> 00:02:36.989
Next, your team building, how are you going
to put a team together?

00:02:36.989 --> 00:02:39.099
How good of a recruiter are you going to be?

00:02:39.099 --> 00:02:46.829
How good are you at bringing solid talent,
operations, systems, sales, technology, compliance,

00:02:46.829 --> 00:02:47.829
how are you going to do that?

00:02:47.829 --> 00:02:48.980
How well are you going to do that?

00:02:48.980 --> 00:02:50.109
Team building.

00:02:50.109 --> 00:02:53.639
You will face that challenge, where you're
going to realize you can't do it all.

00:02:53.639 --> 00:02:55.430
And it comes down to how well you build a
team.

00:02:55.430 --> 00:02:56.680
Next, vision.

00:02:56.680 --> 00:03:00.269
Casting a vision that others want to belong
to.

00:03:00.269 --> 00:03:02.169
Casting a vision where I want to be a part
of.

00:03:02.169 --> 00:03:06.939
You, constantly casting a vision that I can
be a part of it, a year, three years, five

00:03:06.939 --> 00:03:12.499
years, ten years, 20 years down the line,
and my own selfish goals and desires can become

00:03:12.499 --> 00:03:14.669
a reality based on the effort I want to put
in.

00:03:14.669 --> 00:03:19.780
But based on the vision you keep casting that
everybody around you believes because you

00:03:19.780 --> 00:03:23.090
keep getting closer and closer and closer
to that vision.

00:03:23.090 --> 00:03:27.159
If you cannot cast the vision, you're going
to lose the best type of talent, if you don't

00:03:27.159 --> 00:03:28.300
know how to cast the vision.

00:03:28.300 --> 00:03:29.549
Next, you will be lonely.

00:03:29.549 --> 00:03:31.659
I put a song here, Only the Lonely.

00:03:31.659 --> 00:03:33.060
You will be lonely.

00:03:33.060 --> 00:03:35.480
There will be many lonely nights.

00:03:35.480 --> 00:03:38.569
There will be many days where you're going
to sit there by yourself saying, "I don't

00:03:38.569 --> 00:03:40.629
really know if this is going to work out."

00:03:40.629 --> 00:03:42.430
There will be many days you have no one to
call.

00:03:42.430 --> 00:03:48.810
No family, no friend, no girlfriend, no husband,
no wife, no mom, grandma, grandpa, no one

00:03:48.810 --> 00:03:52.930
for you to call because you can't complain
to any of them because you decided to become

00:03:52.930 --> 00:03:54.239
an entrepreneur.

00:03:54.239 --> 00:03:56.299
They never forced you to become an entrepreneur.

00:03:56.299 --> 00:03:57.449
You decided.

00:03:57.449 --> 00:03:59.939
So you call them, the last thing you want
to hear is what?

00:03:59.939 --> 00:04:02.090
I told you not to do it!

00:04:02.090 --> 00:04:04.620
It's going to be a tough phone call.

00:04:04.620 --> 00:04:07.180
So there's going to be many lonely nights.

00:04:07.180 --> 00:04:11.609
Lonely mornings, lonely decision-making process,
lonely Sundays, lonely Saturdays.

00:04:11.609 --> 00:04:14.819
Next, tax and lawyers.

00:04:14.819 --> 00:04:18.180
You are now paying taxes on a new code as
an entrepreneur.

00:04:18.180 --> 00:04:22.720
You will need a CPA that knows how to transition
you from W2 to being an entrepreneur.

00:04:22.720 --> 00:04:25.480
You will need lawyers to protect you from
business.

00:04:25.480 --> 00:04:26.940
How do I structure the company?

00:04:26.940 --> 00:04:31.170
LLC, C Corp, S Corp, you know, is this a Limited
Liability Partnership?

00:04:31.170 --> 00:04:32.170
How am I going to.

00:04:32.170 --> 00:04:34.160
. . am I doing a real-estate partnership with
a group of.

00:04:34.160 --> 00:04:35.420
. . how am I setting this up?

00:04:35.420 --> 00:04:40.280
You're going to need lawyers and taxes, which
means you're going to speak to CPAs and lawyers

00:04:40.280 --> 00:04:44.620
in ways you've probably never dealt before,
and they're going to tell you some stuff that

00:04:44.620 --> 00:04:45.620
you've never heard before.

00:04:45.620 --> 00:04:48.470
Where in many cases you're going to sit there
and act like you know what you're talking

00:04:48.470 --> 00:04:52.560
about, but you have no clue what they're saying,
and you kind of don't want them to think that

00:04:52.560 --> 00:04:55.170
you don't know because they'll charge you
more, but you need to ask.

00:04:55.170 --> 00:04:56.960
I don't understand.

00:04:56.960 --> 00:04:58.510
Can you please explain this to me?

00:04:58.510 --> 00:04:59.510
You will face this.

00:04:59.510 --> 00:05:00.510
It's inevitable.

00:05:00.510 --> 00:05:01.870
Next, you will wear many different hats.

00:05:01.870 --> 00:05:02.870
You're just going to.

00:05:02.870 --> 00:05:04.330
You're going to be a salesperson one day.

00:05:04.330 --> 00:05:05.420
You're going to clean your room one day.

00:05:05.420 --> 00:05:07.750
One day no one's cleaned the kitchen, and
you've got to do it.

00:05:07.750 --> 00:05:09.139
No one's putting the stuff in the files.

00:05:09.139 --> 00:05:10.139
You've got to do it.

00:05:10.139 --> 00:05:11.420
You've got to answer the phones sometimes.

00:05:11.420 --> 00:05:14.160
You've got to get back to a text that you
probably shouldn't be getting back to as a

00:05:14.160 --> 00:05:17.000
CEO, but you need to because you're wearing
many different hats.

00:05:17.000 --> 00:05:18.500
You're going to do design.

00:05:18.500 --> 00:05:20.100
You're going to do what the website looks
like.

00:05:20.100 --> 00:05:21.200
You may do social media.

00:05:21.200 --> 00:05:22.230
You may do the posting.

00:05:22.230 --> 00:05:25.460
No one knows this because you're wearing many
different hats and you have to go through

00:05:25.460 --> 00:05:27.340
it as a person who starts a business.

00:05:27.340 --> 00:05:29.680
Next, I'm going to knock you out.

00:05:29.680 --> 00:05:30.680
You know what this is?

00:05:30.680 --> 00:05:34.190
You're going to deal with people that want
to put your out of business.

00:05:34.190 --> 00:05:37.080
And you're going to say, "how brutal is this?

00:05:37.080 --> 00:05:38.270
You can't be this cold."

00:05:38.270 --> 00:05:39.890
It's the world of business.

00:05:39.890 --> 00:05:42.490
You're taking a piece of business away from
them, and they want to put you out of business.

00:05:42.490 --> 00:05:46.390
So you're going to have a lot of competition
that are going to do whatever they can to

00:05:46.390 --> 00:05:47.650
put you out of business.

00:05:47.650 --> 00:05:49.390
Next one here is lifestyle change.

00:05:49.390 --> 00:05:50.720
This is difficult for a lot of people.

00:05:50.720 --> 00:05:52.080
Let me explain.

00:05:52.080 --> 00:05:54.770
You're accustomed to going out on Friday nights
and Saturday nights.

00:05:54.770 --> 00:05:56.610
And Thursday night ladies' night.

00:05:56.610 --> 00:05:58.050
And maybe sleeping in a little bit.

00:05:58.050 --> 00:06:01.770
And maybe working five o'clock you come home,
you watch all the games, all the playoff games,

00:06:01.770 --> 00:06:04.550
all the soccer matches, all the football games.

00:06:04.550 --> 00:06:07.110
You get every one of those things because
it's your lifestyle.

00:06:07.110 --> 00:06:10.360
Your boys call you on Friday night because
you have this one spot you go to.

00:06:10.360 --> 00:06:13.430
Saturday night is your favorite three lounges
that you go to.

00:06:13.430 --> 00:06:16.220
Sunday you have a spot that you go to from
eight o'clock to one o'clock in the morning,

00:06:16.220 --> 00:06:20.350
and you go to sleep at 1:30, so you can get
some rest to wake up at 7:00 in the morning.

00:06:20.350 --> 00:06:22.440
You have all your spots that you do.

00:06:22.440 --> 00:06:25.960
Let me prepare you, all of this is going to
change.

00:06:25.960 --> 00:06:28.720
Your relationship with some of your friends,
is going to change.

00:06:28.720 --> 00:06:31.710
Your daily habits, are going to change.

00:06:31.710 --> 00:06:34.910
Some of the people that you were hanging out
with before, it's going to change.

00:06:34.910 --> 00:06:38.290
Some of the places you used to go to before,
it's going to change.

00:06:38.290 --> 00:06:41.710
Generally, this most people cannot handle.

00:06:41.710 --> 00:06:46.050
Because they want to win big as an entrepreneur
and become a hero and celebrity and all this

00:06:46.050 --> 00:06:48.090
stuff, but they want to keep this lifestyle.

00:06:48.090 --> 00:06:50.370
So it's almost like they're not letting go
of this to go get this.

00:06:50.370 --> 00:06:54.470
You have to let go of the lifestyle and if
you can't let go of this lifestyle if you

00:06:54.470 --> 00:06:58.210
cannot wear multiple hats, if you cannot understand
the competition's going to want to put you

00:06:58.210 --> 00:07:02.050
out of business, if you don't pay attention
to tax and law, if you don't realize you're

00:07:02.050 --> 00:07:08.190
going to be lonely, if you don't constantly
cast a vision, build a team, process issues,

00:07:08.190 --> 00:07:10.620
know that you don't have a lot of time to
left with the savings that you have, the capital

00:07:10.620 --> 00:07:16.350
that you have, and the fact that you need
to eventually sacrifice your salary, the cushion,

00:07:16.350 --> 00:07:22.200
the warm, fuzzy feeling of a steady salary
coming in, you're going to have a very hard

00:07:22.200 --> 00:07:27.480
time as an entrepreneur and I highly recommend
you don't do anything to become an entrepreneur,

00:07:27.480 --> 00:07:29.060
you stay as an employee.

